================================================================================
2. ALPHAFOLD SERVER MODELS  —  NON-COMMERCIAL, NOT MIT
================================================================================

Applies to these files and anything derived from them:

    new_biology/rnasej_mg_2x2_AF3_model_0.cif
    new_biology/rnasej_mpn_2x2_AF3_model_0.cif
    new_biology/rnasej_mg_2x2_summary_confidences_0.json
    new_biology/rnasej_mpn_2x2_summary_confidences_0.json
    new_biology/rnaseJ_MG139_MG423_heterotetramer_CA.pdb
    rnasej/afserver_rnasej.json

These are AlphaFold Server output. They are redistributed here under the
AlphaFold Server Output Terms of Use, which permit use and publication for
scientific research and expressly FORBID commercial use. The MIT grant in
section 1 does NOT extend to them and could not, because those rights were never
held and so cannot be passed on.

The terms additionally forbid using this output in connection with any automated
system that predicts the binding or interaction of a protein with ligands or
peptides. That prohibition is the entire reason the virtual screen in
`cleanroom/` was built on Boltz-2 (MIT licensed) from public sequences instead,
with no AlphaFold output anywhere in its inputs. See `cleanroom/provenance.json`.

If you want to build something commercial on this work, use the clean-room path
and do not touch these six files.

